---
description: Native Cursor Agent vs Engineering Orchestrator contract
alwaysApply: true
---

Cursor Agent is the interactive engineering UI for this Product repository.
Native reads, search, edits, and focused tests are normal. Do not treat a
previous chat transcript as Change Unit authority.

The Engineering Orchestrator (EO) owns the durable Change Unit lifecycle,
fresh sibling worktree/bootstrap, TYPED_IMPORT environment, test-instance/UAT
authority, formal validation sequencing, and commit/release/deploy/canary.
When an EO Change Unit exists, call public `CONTINUE_CHANGE_UNIT` / `eo
change-unit continue` instead of recreating lifecycle, worktrees, or env by
hand. Resume from EO durable CU artifacts after Open Folder.
Chat transcript is not lifecycle authority; chat continuity is not promised.

Do not manually create Product worktrees as an EO substitute. Do not
wholesale-copy `.env`; use the EO TYPED_IMPORT contract and machine-local
overlay/source references. Tracked `.eo/repository-profile.json` is Product
metadata, not a second orchestrator.

UAT precedes formal validation. A standing through-production grant removes
routine repeated release approvals on the standard path. Hard exceptional
safety (production access, secrets, destructive Git, non-standard deploy)
still requires explicit authority.

Explicit prompt override beats EO defaults. Hard execution safety remains
highest.
